    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d237">

                <pb facs="0200" n="196" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg196"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/14278: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-11-03T12:00:00+00:00">November 3,
                        1938—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received November 3—9:22 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1856. Your 828, November 2, 3 p.m.<anchor n="58" xml:id="d237-f1"/> I have just
                    discussed this question with Hoppenot, Chief of the Far Eastern Division at the
                    Foreign Office. He stated that he was glad that we were taking this matter up
                    with the Japanese Government and was also glad that we were informing the French
                    Government in advance in order that they might have an opportunity to take
                    similar action.</p>
                <p>The French have only two or three ships on the Yangtze but these have encountered
                    all manner of obstacles from the Japanese. Hoppe-not stated that the Foreign
                    Office will cable instructions today to the French Ambassador at Tokyo to
                    consult with his American and British colleagues and to take similar but
                    separate action. Repeated to London.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d237-f1" n="58" xml:id="d237-f1-content">
                <p>See last paragraph of telegram No. 672, November 2, 3 p.m., to the Ambassador in
                    the United Kingdom, <ref target="#pg194">p. 194</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
